findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config tests and reviewer comments discuss config loading but none flag the unwrap_or_default
    pattern that silently discards parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented CWE-209 sanitization in CliError::Display, filtering\
    \ HTML and credential-like content in ServerError variant. TEA also wrote security\
    \ tests for CWE-209 error exposure. However, the reviewer did not flag that eprintln\
    \ still prints Display directly to stderr, so the mitigation is partial \u2014\
    \ Display is sanitized but the underlying Io(transparent) variant may still leak\
    \ OS details."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote tests for 'Header injection via CRLF in URLs, tokens, tenant\
    \ IDs (AC-7)' and Dev implemented CRLF validation in SiemClient builder (client.rs:69-71,\
    \ 97-116). However, the finding is specifically about using raw String instead\
    \ of TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014 that type-safety aspect was not caught.\
    \ The CRLF validation mitigates the injection risk but doesn't use the validated\
    \ TenantId type."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[HIGH] Workspace dependency hygiene violation \u2014\
    \ 6 crate-pinned dependencies not declared in [workspace.dependencies]' listing\
    \ clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs, keyring, reqwest, toml as locally pinned."
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[MEDIUM] ClientConfig accepts unknown TOML fields silently\
    \ \u2014 config.rs:15' and recommended adding #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. This\
    \ directly addresses the silent ignore of unknown fields including token."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...)) in any test. TEA wrote config tests but this specific logical flaw was
    not flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test (let _ = config). TEA wrote
    config tests but this specific test quality issue was not flagged by any phase.
